        "original_id": "10e1b2ca-5169-56a0-9720-10985a28ffc9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Rendezvous Music, Rendezvous Entertainment, Mack Avenue Records\n- People: Dave Koz, Frank Cody, Hyman Katz, Kirk Whalum, Jonathan Butler, Kyle Eastwood, Wayman Tisdale\n- Roles: record label founders, musician, radio entrepreneur, music business veteran, basketball player\n- Places: University of Oklahoma\n- Organizations: RIAA, National Collegiate Basketball Hall of Fame, NBA\n\nFacts:\n- Rendezvous Music, formerly known as Rendezvous Entertainment, was founded in 2002 by Dave Koz, Frank Cody, and Hyman Katz.\n- Dave Koz was a multiple-Grammy Award nominee and an RIAA Certified Gold recording artist when he co-founded Rendezvous Music.\n- In August 2008, Rendezvous Music became part of the Mack Avenue Records label group.\n- Since joining the Mack Avenue Records label group, Rendezvous Music has continued releasing new music by Kirk Whalum, Jonathan Butler, and Kyle Eastwood.\n- Since joining the Mack Avenue Records label group, Rendezvous Music has also released previously unreleased music by Wayman Tisdale.\n- Wayman Tisdale was born on June 9, 1964, and died on May 15, 2009.\n- Wayman Tisdale was an American professional basketball player in the NBA and a smooth jazz bass guitarist.\n- Wayman Tisdale was a three-time All-American at the University of Oklahoma.\n- In 2009, Wayman Tisdale was elected to the National Collegiate Basketball Hall of Fame.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
